      "version": "2.6.6",
      "params": [],
      "data": {
        "text": "TriggerFish diode ladder playable smoke test\n\nSETUP\nSelect MIDI and audio devices in MIDI-CV and Audio-8. Start with monitor volume low.\n\nMIDI pitch drives a Fundamental VCO and the filter's V/OCT input. MIDI gate drives the filter's internal TB-303 envelopes and OTA VCA. The VCO saw passes through TfDiodeLadderFilter; LP OUT bypasses the VCA, while VCA OUT is the playable voice used here.\n\nAll TriggerFish parameters are at their declared defaults. Try DRIVE, BASS, high resonance, ACCENT from a sequencer, and the oversampling and articulation context-menu settings. The final VCA Mix is the master, set to -6 dB and routed to outputs 1/2."
      },
      "pos": [
        0,
        0
      ]
    },
